{"type":"message","id":"215e7434","parentId":"77a03086","timestamp":"2026-03-31T13:43:05.566Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] Yes — this second test confirms it.\n\nThe response is again only giving:\n- upload metadata\n- prototype/workflow structure\n- input/data-reader tracking\n\nAnd again it is **not** giving:\n- skin cancer class\n- confidence\n- image analyzer prediction\n- CAM metrics\n- X-AI summary/recommendations\n\nThe strongest evidence is that in this second run too:\n- `skin_cancer_detection_model` has `executed: false`\n- `image_analyzer_model` has `executed: false`\n- `x_ai_model` has `executed: false`\n- their `tracking.metrics` objects are empty\n\nSo yes: based on two separate image tests, the current endpoint response does **not contain anything clinically useful from the downstream models**.\n\nIf you want, I can save this second output too and then inspect the skin pipeline template/script to find why those nodes are not executing.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_095d3f15b185f2f80169cbcf6427b88191ac36812ecba7de14\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":45209,"output":193,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":45402,"cost":{"input":0.11302250000000001,"output":0.002895,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.1159175}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774964577816}}
